  "version": "1.0",
  "description": "Anima Base v1.0 txt2img is a text to image workflow designed to turn a text prompt into a finished still image using Anima Base 1.0. Its 12-node graph exposes 2 prompt/text field(s), 0 media input target(s), and 1 save/preview stage(s), while preserving the original editor-format graph for reference. The ComfyUI editor graph was converted to API format and is ready for live validation against the connected node and model registry.",
  "category": "Image Generation",
  "subcategory": "Text to image",
  "episode": "EP20",
  "instructions": "1. Open the workflow and select Validate. SineForge will compare every node class and input against the currently connected ComfyUI instance without queueing it.\n2. Review the model-file entries in Requirements and place each checkpoint, text encoder, VAE, LoRA, or auxiliary model in the folder documented by the source workflow. Refresh ComfyUI after adding files.\n3. No required media file was detected in the converted graph; begin with the prompt and generation controls.\n4. Edit the positive/negative prompt, resolution, sampler, steps, guidance, and seed. Use a fixed seed while tuning composition, then vary it deliberately.\n5. Save a copy before making structural changes. Use Editable inputs for normal parameters and Raw API JSON only when you need to inspect or change graph wiring.\n6. Validate again after every change. Queue one workflow only after validation passes; then inspect the returned output, logs, duration, dimensions, and media integrity.",
  "tags": [
    "Anima Base 1.0",
    "EP20",
    "Image Generation",
    "Text to image"
  ],
